Namely (1.) by Pride of life, or ambition, clinging for the most part even to the sacred order (as is clear in the Pharisees, Matt. 23:5–7), most hostile to Truth and Peace (John 5:44 & 7:18), and most fertile of quarrels (2 Tim. 3:1–3). As is also plain from that common saying against quarrelsome Arius:
The question is asked why the heretic (schismatic) Arius was made what he was;
The cause is ready at hand: he was ambitious.
